language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session2_movie_scheduling: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ You are an actor offered roles in n movie projects. Each offer has a first and last day of filming, and you must be available throughout that whole period, so you cannot accept two offers whose intervals overlap. Every film pays the same fee, so choose the largest possible set of offers whose intervals pairwise do not conflict. Which movies are accepted?
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `session2_movie_scheduling.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session2_movie_scheduling.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `session2_movie_scheduling_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py session2_movie_scheduling.json
$   savilerow model.eprime session2_movie_scheduling_1.param -run-solver

$ movies_2_dim1: the number of movie offers (derived by the converter from the data)
given movies_2_dim1 : int
letting n_movies = movies_2_dim1
$ movies_2[i]: first filming day of movie i (indices 1-based; the second column of the data's movies list)
given movies_2 : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_movies)] of int
$ movies_3[i]: last filming day of movie i (the third column of the data's movies list)
given movies_3 : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_movies)] of int

$ selected_movies[i]: movie i is accepted
find selected_movies : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_movies)] of bool
$ n_selected: auxiliary, the number of movies accepted
find n_selected : int(0..n_movies)

$ search hint: branch on the accepted movies first (speeds up the search)
branching on [selected_movies]

maximising n_selected

such that
$ the number of accepted movies is the number of selected movies
n_selected = (sum i : int(1..n_movies) . toInt(selected_movies[i])),
$ two movies whose filming intervals overlap cannot both be accepted; intervals overlap when each starts on or before the day the other ends
forAll i, j : int(1..n_movies) . (i < j /\ movies_2[i] <= movies_3[j] /\ movies_2[j] <= movies_3[i]) -> (!selected_movies[i] \/ !selected_movies[j])
